{"acceptance_length": 3.9833333333333334, "acceptance_lengths": [1, 1, 7, 2, 7, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3, 1, 8, 4, 2, 2, 4, 6, 2, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 4, 1, 3, 2, 7, 4, 7, 8, 8, 8, 8, 4, 1, 1, 8, 5, 1, 8, 7, 3, 7, 3, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 6, 2], "accepted_draft_lengths": [0, 0, 6, 1, 6, 1, 2, 0, 1, 2, 0, 7, 3, 1, 1, 3, 5, 1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3, 0, 2, 1, 6, 3, 6, 7, 7, 7, 7, 3, 0, 0, 7, 4, 0, 7, 6, 2, 6, 2, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 5, 1], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23086297088, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23086287872, "benchmark": "mbpp", "completion": "To solve this, we need to understand the formula for the **nth octagonal number**.\n\n### Formula for the nth Octagonal Number:\nThe nth octagonal number is given by the formula:\n\n$$\nO_n = n(3n - 2)\n$$\n\nThis formula gives the number of dots in a pattern of dots that forms an octagon.\n\n---\n\n### Example:\nFor $ n = 5 $:\n$$\nO_5 = 5(3 \\cdot 5 - 2) = 5(15 - 2) = 5 \\cdot 13 = 65\n$$\n\nWhich matches the assertion `is_octagonal(5) == 65`.\n\n---\n\n### Python Function:\n\n```python\ndef is_octagonal(n):\n    return n * (3 * n - 2)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Test Cases:\n\n```python\nassert is_octagonal(5) == 65\nassert is_octagonal(10) == 280\nassert is_octagonal(15) == 645\n```\n\nAll of these will pass with the above function.\n\n\u2705 **Your code is correct.**", "decode_seconds": 3.3623019717633724, "draft_calls": 60, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 89, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "bd20c784e546e8778a6062a600364411a7c946387693eb0712123eae85d2a6e5", "method": "relay_math_2layers", "output_hash": "6e51faf85db0198aed13971b3cb6f204c08f6c9a622e061ab721eee0b4df2bbd", "output_tokens": 240, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23190068224, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23406313472, "problem_id": "Mbpp/59", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 1410.9570885896683, "prefill_full_target": 33.11110305786133, "prefill_relay": 0.19897599518299103, "relay": 9.707616001367569, "unattributed_runtime": 48.30120812